{
  "_what": "The Source's springs: one per repository whose commit feed stimpunks.org's feeds page lists under Latest Commits to Our Repositories, in that page's order (https://stimpunks.org/feeds/). The order is that page's, decided there, and is not re-sorted here. tools/pull-source.py fills `items` and `read` off each feed and `set` for the whole terrace; tools/make-the-source.py draws the pools out of it and writes the springs into netlify/cb/lib.mjs for the feed bot. Hand-kept: id, site, repo, home, feed and note, the last of which is our own line about what the repository is for.",
  "_skip": "The morning timers' own commits, left off the pools and off the room's channel: a machine re-reading feeds is not anybody's work, and the Knowledge System's update-logs skips the same subjects. make-the-source.py refuses this pattern unless it matches every subject tools/daily-*.sh commits under, so a new timer cannot quietly flood the terraces.",
  "skip": "^daily [a-z ]+$",
